  "published": "2026-11-25T22:59:42.267Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "ADDED\n- `CollectDeviceIdentifiers()` sets the device's identifiers as subscriber attributes of the current user, which attribution integrations such as RevenueCat's Meta Ads integration use for matching. Call it after `Initialize`; getting the user's consent before calling it is your responsibility.\n  - iOS and Mac Catalyst: `$idfa`, `$idfv`, `$ip` and `$deviceVersion`. `$idfa` needs your app to link the AdSupport framework, and from iOS 14.5 the user's App Tracking Transparency authorization.\n  - Android: `$gpsAdId`, `$ip` and `$deviceVersion`.\n  - Windows and other platforms: the call does nothing.\n\nNOTE\n- Your own implementation of `IRevenueCatBilling`, if you have one, needs the new member. Nothing else in `IRevenueCatBilling` or its DTOs changed, and the bindings are the same as in 10.1.0.",
